# .dockerignore excluded the lockfile → `failed to compute cache key`

## TL;DR

`docker build` failed with `failed to compute cache key: "/package-lock.json" not found`
even though the file existed on disk. Cause: a broad `.dockerignore` pattern
(`*.json`) excluded the lockfile from the build context, so `COPY package*.json ./`
could never match it. Fix: narrow the ignore rule, keep the lockfile in the context.

## Environment

| Item | Value |
| --- | --- |
| OS | Ubuntu 24.04.1 LTS (also reproduced on macOS 14.6 arm64) |
| Docker Engine | 27.2.1 (build 9e8f3f2), BuildKit v0.15.2 |
| Node | 20.17.0 |
| npm | 10.8.2 |
| Repo state | monorepo, `Dockerfile` at repo root, `.dockerignore` at repo root |

